  "question": {
    "text": "In the triangle <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>, vertices <math><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>C</mi></math> are <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3,1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1,6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> respectively. If the internal angle bisector of <math><mi>∠</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> meets <math><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> at <math><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the coordinates of <math><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "tWn7s",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "lqznM",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2Nucg",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HgW0V",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math>, <math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>20</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;is the internal angle bisector,&nbsp;<br />so <math><mi>D</mi></math> divides <math><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> in the ratio of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now, applying section formula, we get,<br />The coordinates of&nbsp;<math><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>≡</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
